# data/ holds all user-owned transactional content: sessions, records, attachments.
# Contributors should not commit their personal data here.
#
# IMPORTANT FOR PERSONAL INSTANCES: remove the line below so your data is tracked.
# Claude web and Claude Code read session state, records, and attachments from the
# repo — without git tracking, your history is invisible to the AI.
# .gitignore is NOT in sync scope, so removing this line is safe across syncs.
data/
